  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps the 5% ceiling and gives purchasers full per-model results but removes any automatic sales stop: exceeding 5% triggers review and retesting, with an open-ended regulator-set timeline, which favours Northwind's 6.2% Hearth 10. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which is triggered by Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, so it costs Halcyon directly. S3's 6-year retrofit and S4's 36-month suppression deadline sit inside the acceptable ranges, and the S3 new-unit deadline is a calendar date (1 January 2028) with no stated adoption-relative month count, so it is recorded as null."
